Masha leads the [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Golden Sparrows]]. She is a dwarf of platinum skin with hair and eyes of bright gold, and she wears the plain working clothes of anyone in the city. She does not blink or breathe that a watcher can see, and her face does not move; to a mage she reads as magic older and greater than a person's. When she comes and goes the air presses past like water moving around a swimmer.

She wants [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] free of its government, which she holds tramples the powerless. She has counted herself ready for the change that would follow, and has said she will help rebuild after. She once asked [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] for aid and broke contact when she found the strings attached, and the Playwrights are part of why she is as she is. She knows nothing of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the creature from below]].

She gave the Weft a matchstick: snapped, it severs the holder from cause and effect for a few seconds, sparing them anything short of an artifact.

Her word reaches the movement through [[People/Althane/Wojciech|Wojciech]].
